<title>INDIA: Indian soybean firm on good demand, poor supply.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean firm on good demand, poor supply.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices were firm on Friday on good demand from processing plants and poor arrivals, traders said.</p>
<p>They said prices rose by 100-150 rupees per tonne.</p>
<p>Soyoil solvent was up by 100 rupees per tonne on good demand from refineries while soyoil refined was steady, traders said.</p>
<p>They said volumes were low and the undertone steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were steady in thin trade. Soymeal yellow was $270-271 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $136 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,550 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,500-4,525 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
